Third-party material

Two golden LedgerCloseMeta files from stellar-core v30.0.0 (https://github.com/stellar/stellar-core,
commit 0e49751aa9ddf892302cca02cea7f3f5d97df9f1, Apache License 2.0, copyright Stellar Development
Foundation and contributors) are used as test fixtures in
crates/shapekit-core-driver/tests/fixtures/core-golden/, unmodified:
  test-lcm-current/InvokeHostFunctionTests/a61f6dd6f81e6f17.xdr
  test-lcm-current/BeginSponsoringFutureReservesTests/1467a37ff2a1e960.xdr

Twelve golden LedgerCloseMeta files from the same stellar-core v30.0.0 commit are used,
unmodified, as test fixtures in crates/shapekit-oracle/tests/fixtures/core-goldens/. Each file's
upstream path under test-lcm-current/, test case and SHA-256 are listed in
crates/shapekit-oracle/tests/fixtures/provenance.json.

Golden LedgerCloseMeta values from stellar-core v30.0.0 (https://github.com/stellar/stellar-core,
commit 0e49751aa9ddf892302cca02cea7f3f5d97df9f1, Apache License 2.0, copyright Stellar Development
Foundation and contributors) are imported, unmodified, as corpus entries with source class
core-golden under corpus/entries/. Each such entry names its upstream file under
test-lcm-current/ and that file's SHA-256 in its entry.json, and corpus/goldens/core-v30.0.0/index.json
lists every upstream golden file with its SHA-256 and the entries imported from it.

Reduced excerpts of stellar/wallet-backend (https://github.com/stellar/wallet-backend, Apache
License 2.0, copyright Stellar Development Foundation and contributors) are used, modified, as
linter test data in lint/idx001/testdata/src/walletbackend/, lint/idx002/testdata/src/walletbackend/
and lint/idx003/testdata/src/walletbackend/. They are cut down from
internal/indexer/processors/contract_operations.go, internal/indexer/processors/contract_deploy.go,
internal/indexer/processors/state_change_builder.go and internal/indexer/types/types.go at commits
79ea2acd1dc65a07166133cc04b12e76db314db0, 9538b3caeaebfeb3d034146c0ce9643c3066cf8a,
f8e5786d22c04adad16318f2e126728beec5aac9 and e967ce8b7362b79c277e700e789181d76fbb5967. Each file,
or each function in it, names the upstream file and commit it was taken from and says that it
was reduced or adapted.

The files schema/xdr/<tag>/xdr.json are generated from the XDR definitions of stellar/stellar-xdr
(https://github.com/stellar/stellar-xdr, Apache License 2.0, copyright Stellar Development
Foundation and contributors) at the stellar-xdr ref each directory names, by the
generator-definitions-json program of stellar/rs-stellar-xdr
(https://github.com/stellar/rs-stellar-xdr, Apache License 2.0, copyright Stellar Development
Foundation and contributors) at commit 3c2aa43d2ab54d429ae44aa5143d805bf5dba7e2.
scripts/fetch-xdr-definitions.sh writes them. Each file lists its source .x files with their
SHA-256 and quotes the definitions' source text.
